{
  "burst_aware_sizing_rule": "For each delivery probability p and Wilson half-width, packets_bursty = ceil(F * packets_independent), where rho = 1 - burst_p - burst_r and F = (1 + rho) / (1 - rho); this is a large-n approximation for the two-state chain. Here p is the delivery probability used by the Wilson table, while burst_p is the Good-to-Bad transition probability. With loss_good=0 and loss_bad=1, the chain's stationary delivery is burst_r / (burst_p + burst_r) = 0.9090909. The table's delivery p values do not equal this stationary delivery; the inflation factor is still the chain's own.",
